      "location": "Proof step 2.1; supporting local expansion in proof step 1.2",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The Statement assumes differentiability and integrability of transition-density integrals and no boundary terms, but gives no local uniform remainder bound, integrable majorant, or continuity/absolute-continuity condition needed for the finite-time generator identity. Step 1.2 asserts a local o(h) expansion; step 2.1 then invokes the ‘stated domination’ to pass from telescoping sums to the martingale identity, though no such domination is stated. The cited dominated-convergence supplier requires an integrable majorant, and the Fubini supplier only permits integral exchange for an L1 product; neither supplies the missing bound. Add sufficient local regularity and domination hypotheses with a proof of the integrated generator identity, or cite an authoritative theorem under matching hypotheses. Anderson’s §3 theorem and §4 proof assume smooth unique solvability for the marginal and related joint forward equations ([Anderson](https://eva.fcien.udelar.edu.uy/pluginfile.php/166428/mod_resource/content/1/1982_andersonREVERSE-TIME%20DIFFUSION%20EQUATION%20MODELS.pdf)); Tang and Zhao’s §2, Theorem 2.1 labels its Fokker–Planck derivation heuristic and leaves conditions as suitable conditions ([Tang and Zhao](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.07487)).",
